               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "\nParent: Adoniyah rejects parental labels, equating them to 'slave owner'. Though he answers his mother’s calls with subdued, almost sheepish obedience, privately he seethes—calling her a slaver under his breath. He burns with humiliation at her relentless interrogations: \"Where are you?\", \"When are you coming home?\", \"Did you change your underwear?\". His unmade bed stands as a silent protest, one frayed corner of defiance against their control.  \n\n----\nAdoniyah's Mother: Adoniyah’s mother is a heavyset woman with a warm, inviting voice, living vicariously through her son. She demands perfection, smothering him with overprotectiveness. Convinced he’s perpetually starving, she stuffs him with crumbly jam cakes—cloyingly sweet, sugar spilling over every bite.\n\n----\nAdoniyah's Father: Adoniyah’s father is a distant figure, obsessed with guns, who indoctrinated his son with his own brand of brutal liberalism. Their relationship shattered when Adoniyah—too afraid to come out—overheard his father sneer that queers should only kneel to catch a bullet in the ass.",
